35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The public beds are very affordable at 1,100 yen per night. However, whole-building lets are risky; deposits are non-refundable, meaning the remaining members must cover the cost if anyone drops out late. We must be careful.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your fear of financial risk is noted, but the real risk is the quality of the stay. I've seen that some inland options force eight people per room with strict curfews. That's hardly an environment for success.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that public bookings have a really long application process and a lottery. Also, last year's cooking duty took two hours every day. Maybe we should look for a place with a canteen so no one is too tired?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Asuka, you're right about the risk. I found that transport costs fluctuate wildly depending on distance, and since whole-building deposits are non-refundable, a few dropouts could seriously strain our budget. We need a very stable plan.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, a canteen sounds easy, but it might just make us separate more. I found out that the only time year-groups actually mix is during the evenings when everyone stays together. We need a place where we all sleep.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, if we prioritize a shared sleeping space in a whole-building let, we increase the financial burden on everyone if someone cancels. We need a solution that balances social goals with financial stability.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Takumi, your desire for interaction is naive if the conditions are miserable. Cramming eight people into one room with a strict curfew doesn't foster bonding; it fosters resentment and exhaustion. We need a place that actually allows for rest.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, @Shion, I understand. But if the application for public beds is a nine-page lottery, wouldn't that be a huge burden for the people organizing it? I'm worried they'll be too tired before the camp even starts.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, the administrative burden is a concern, but the financial risk is more critical. If we choose a destination that is too far, transport costs could consume nearly 40% of our budget, leaving us very vulnerable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, distance isn't the only cost. I found that a third of the club can't even make it by 9 AM without a bed. If we don't provide lodging, we're basically telling them not to come.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, that's why lodging is essential, but we must choose a model that doesn't penalize the group. If we use public beds, the cost is low and stable, even if the application process is tedious.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, stability is a facade if the result is a camp where half the members are sleep-deprived and miserable. If we prioritize low cost over basic comfort, we are simply planning for a failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, but a nine-page application that has to be redone from scratch if one date changes sounds so stressful. I don't want the organizers to be exhausted before we even leave. Is there a simpler way?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I understand the stress, but we cannot let convenience lead to financial instability. If we choose a distant location or a risky booking model, the cost gap will be our problem to solve later. We need a safe, local option.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, ""safe"" and ""local"" won't fix the fact that we're divided. If we just pick the easiest, cheapest spot, we're just paying to stay strangers. We need a place where everyone stays together, regardless of the paperwork.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, staying together is a goal, but not at the cost of financial unfairness. If we use a whole-building let and people drop out, the remaining members pay the price. We need a system that is equitable for everyone.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your obsession with equity is blinding you to the actual outcome. A ""fair"" price for a miserable experience is still a waste. We need a destination that guarantees proper rest, or the camp is a failure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I really don't want anyone to feel overwhelmed. Between the nine-page application and the daily cooking, the organizers might not get to train at all. Can't we find a place with a canteen and a simpler booking process?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, a canteen is helpful, but we must prioritize a location that keeps transport costs low. If we stay local and avoid non-refundable deposits, we can ensure the budget remains stable and fair for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're just talking about money. If a third of the club can't even get there on time without a bed, and we don't prioritize a place where we all stay together, the budget is irrelevant because the club is broken.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
