60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is the most logical. It is affordable and avoids the non-refundable deposit risks of Option C. While the application is tedious, it ensures financial equity and provides the shared lodging @Takumi wants.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, Option A is a trap. Public facilities often mean cramped dorms and strict rules, which leads to sleep deprivation. If we prioritize a ""logical"" price over actual rest, we're just paying for a collective nightmare.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, I'm really worried about Option A. The nine-page application and the lottery sound so stressful for the organizers. Also, Option C has meals arranged, so no one has to spend hours cooking!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, Option C is too risky. It's two prefectures away, meaning transport costs will be huge, and the whole-building let means we're liable for any dropouts. We cannot afford that kind of financial instability.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, Option B is a joke. If we stay on campus, we'll just go home or stick to our usual cliques. We need Option A or C to actually force us to spend the evenings together.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, Option A achieves your goal of shared lodging without the financial danger of Option C. @Minato, the administrative effort is a one-time cost, whereas a budget deficit from dropouts is a lasting burden on the members.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, you're ignoring the human cost. Cramming people into dorms leads to the same exhaustion I've seen before. Option B is the only logical choice; it guarantees a controlled environment where we can actually prioritize recovery and performance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shion, but Option B doesn't solve the cooking problem! If we stay on campus, the canteen is closed, so someone will have to spend hours cooking every day. That's not a controlled environment; it's just more work for the organizers.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, the cooking burden is a problem, but Option C's distance and booking terms are far worse. Option B is the safest for the budget, but if we must leave campus, Option A is the only financially responsible choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, Option B is just a glorified practice session. If we don't leave campus, we're not having a camp; we're just staying in our bubbles. Option A is the only way to actually fix this club.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, @Minato, the administrative burden and dorm conditions are manageable compared to the risk of financial unfairness. Option A provides the necessary shared environment while keeping costs low and stable for everyone. It is the most balanced choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, ""manageable"" is a word used by people who aren't the ones losing sleep. If we choose Option A, we are choosing a facility that prioritizes capacity over quality. I cannot support a plan that guarantees exhaustion.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, I can't agree. The organizers already have so much to do, and a nine-page application is just too much. Option C is the only one where no one has to struggle with cooking or paperwork.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, Option C is a financial gamble we cannot take. The transport costs alone would be astronomical. If we want to avoid stress, we should avoid the risk of a budget deficit. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, Option C is a gamble that could bankrupt us. @Shion, I don't care about ""perfect"" sleep if we're all strangers. Option A is the only one that forces us together and keeps it affordable. I vote A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Minato, @Shion, while your concerns are valid, the risk of financial instability and unfair costs in Option C or the social failure of Option B are greater. Option A is the only equitable and effective choice. I vote A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your ""equitable"" choice is a recipe for burnout. I refuse to endorse a destination that sacrifices the members' physical well-being for the sake of a spreadsheet. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I really don't want the organizers to be exhausted by paperwork or cooking. Option A and B both sound too stressful for them. Even if it's a gamble, I want everyone to be happy. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, happiness cannot be built on a financial deficit. We must be realistic about our funds to protect the club's future. Option A is the only responsible way to meet our goals. I vote A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, @Minato, you're both missing the point. A camp that doesn't fix our division is a failure, and a camp that bankrupts us is a disaster. Option A is the only real solution. I vote A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
